.TH FERMI_SSO_COOKIES 1 "2026-09-16" "requests-fermi-sso 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fermi_sso_cookies \- list the cookies held in a saved single sign\-on jar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fermi_sso_cookies
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fermi_sso_cookies
reads a cookie jar and prints one line per cookie: domain, path, name, time
to expiry, the secure/httponly/host\-only flags, and a masked value. A jar
written by
.BR FermiSSOSession (3)
or by
.BR fermi_sso_probe (1)
is the only state a cookies\-only run has, so when such a run fails the
first question is what the file actually holds and whether the identity
provider or service provider session in it has expired. This tool answers
that without touching the network.
.PP
All three jar formats the library understands are read:
.B netscape
(a browser's
.IR cookies.txt ),
.B lwp
(Set\-Cookie3), and
.BR json .
The format is detected from the file extension and first line, as
.B FermiSSOSession.load_cookies
does, or forced with
.BR \-\-cookie\-format .
.PP
Unlike
.BR load_cookies ,
which silently skips expired cookies, every cookie in the file is listed.
Each is assigned a state:
.RS
.TP
.B live
has an expiry more than fifteen minutes away
.TP
.B soon
expires within fifteen minutes
.TP
.B session
has no expiry; kept for the browser's, or the jar's, lifetime
.TP
.B expired
past its expiry and would not be loaded
.RE
.PP
Cookie values are bearer credentials, so by default only the first four
characters and the length are printed.
.B \-\-show\-values
prints them in full. Output goes to standard output; the file header and
summary are omitted with
.BR \-\-quiet .
The tool also warns when the jar is readable by group or other.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I FILE
The jar to read. May also be given as
.BR "\-c FILE" ,
or via
.B $FERMI_SSO_COOKIE_FILE
or an env file, with the usual precedence.
.TP
.BI \-c " FILE" "\fR, \fP" \-\-cookie\-file " FILE"
Same as the positional
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BI \-\-cookie\-format " FORMAT"
One of
.BR netscape ", " lwp ", " json .
Default: detect.
.TP
.BI \-e " FILE" "\fR, \fP" \-\-env\-file " FILE"
Load settings from
.IR FILE .
Default:
.I ./.env
then
.IR ~/.fermi_sso.env ,
the same search
.BR fermi_sso_probe (1)
performs, so a probe configuration names the jar for this tool too.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-env\-file
Ignore env files entirely.
.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-long
One labelled block per cookie, with the absolute expiry timestamp.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Machine\-readable JSON: the file, the detected format, the generation time,
state counts, and a list of cookie records with epoch expiries and a
.B remaining
field in seconds (negative once expired).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-show\-values
Print cookie values in full.
.TP
.B \-\-utc
With
.BR \-\-long ,
show expiry timestamps in UTC rather than local time.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Omit the file header, summary, and permissions warning.
.SS Filters
Filters of different kinds AND together; repeated filters of the same kind
OR together.
.TP
.BI \-D " DOMAIN" "\fR, \fP" \-\-domain " DOMAIN"
Only cookies for
.I DOMAIN
or a subdomain of it. Leading dots are ignored, so
.B fnal.gov
selects
.IR .fnal.gov ", " pingprod.fnal.gov " and " mu2e\-docdb.fnal.gov .
A shell\-style glob is matched literally against the domain instead.
Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-N " NAME" "\fR, \fP" \-\-name " NAME"
Only cookies whose name matches the glob
.IR NAME .
Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-live
Only cookies
.B FermiSSOSession
would actually load: the live, soon and session states.
.TP
.B \-\-expired
Only cookies past their expiry.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FERMI_SSO_COOKIE_FILE
Default jar path, as for
.IR FILE .
.TP
.B FERMI_SSO_COOKIE_FORMAT
Default format, as for
.BR \-\-cookie\-format .
.TP
.B FERMI_SSO_ENV_FILE
Path to the env file, overriding the default search.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./.env
.TQ
.I ~/.fermi_sso.env
Env files searched in that order when
.B \-\-env\-file
is not given. Only the two cookie settings above are read from them.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
At least one cookie was listed.
.TP
.B 1
The jar was read but no cookie survived the filters (or the jar is empty).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: no jar named, a missing or unparseable jar, a missing env
file, or an unknown format.
.SH EXAMPLES
List the jar the probe has been maintaining:
.PP
.RS
.EX
fermi_sso_cookies ~/.fermi_sso.cookies
.EE
.RE
.PP
Typical output:
.PP
.RS
.EX
file    : /home/me/.fermi_sso.cookies
format  : netscape
cookies : 3 total, 1 live, 1 session, 1 expired

DOMAIN               PATH  NAME           EXPIRES            FLAGS                      VALUE
mu2e\-docdb.fnal.gov  /     mellon\-cookie  session            secure,httponly,host\-only  d1f4\(bu (32 chars)
old.fnal.gov         /     stale          expired 2h 0m ago  secure,host\-only           **** (4 chars)
pingprod.fnal.gov    /     PF             in 7h 12m          secure,httponly,host\-only  Kq9z\(bu (28 chars)
.EE
.RE
.PP
Is the identity provider session still good? Show only pingprod's cookies,
in full:
.PP
.RS
.EX
fermi_sso_cookies \-D pingprod.fnal.gov \-l \-s ~/.fermi_sso.cookies
.EE
.RE
.PP
Check a browser export before handing it to the probe, using the jar named
in the probe's env file:
.PP
.RS
.EX
fermi_sso_cookies \-\-live \-e ~/.fermi_sso.env
.EE
.RE
.PP
Feed the expired cookies to another tool:
.PP
.RS
.EX
fermi_sso_cookies \-j \-\-expired ~/.fermi_sso.cookies | jq \-r '.cookies[].name'
.EE
.RE
.PP
Exit status alone, for a script that decides whether to re\-login:
.PP
.RS
.EX
if ! fermi_sso_cookies \-q \-\-live \-D pingprod.fnal.gov \-N PF "$JAR" >/dev/null; then
    fermi_sso_probe \-\-env\-file ~/.fermi_sso.env \-c "$JAR" \-n \-q
fi
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fermi_sso_probe (1),
.BR FermiSSOSession (3)
.PP
Project documentation:
.I docs/HOWTO.md
in the source distribution.
.SH AUTHOR
Utility added for the Mu2e DocDB authentication work.
